The new name is not only an abbreviation for the rapper’s current stage name – according to previous revelations, it also has religious significance for West.
“I’m aware that ‘Yele’ is the most commonly used word in the Bible, and in the bible it’s meant ‘you,’” West said earlier when he talked about the title of his album with Big Boy radio presenter.
“So it’s you and me and we’re all one.
The Kanye means the only one, and from this it became Ye, which symbolizes the good, the bad, the confusion, everything.
“The album reflects who we really are.”
