“It’s not just Toyota, but also other manufacturers that we definitely need to keep our fast-paced supply chain.”
Toyota has not been able to say how long the production would last, but has warned that the cumulative costs could deteriorate the factory’s competitiveness in the long run, which could eventually result in job losses.
According to Peter Tsouvallaris, who has worked at the Burnaston plant for 24 years and is currently a member of the Unite trade union, trade union members are becoming more and more concerned: “According to my experience, we will never get the jobs that have been lost again.”
